      "unparseable_genuinely_malformed": 4
    },
    "what": "combine_humaneval_prompt() (archived driver, reproduced verbatim) indents the raw output by 4 spaces under the prompt whenever the raw has no top-level 'def'. DreamOn already emits a 4-space-indented body, so the stitch double-indents it -> SyntaxError. This is why HE+ parseability falls to .287 at canvas=128 while MBPP+ (which uses extract_python, no stitching) stays at .984. A dedent-aware stitch would restore 158/164 parseable at canvas=128. The bug is shared with the archived runs, so it does not break comparability, but it means HE+ pass@1 at large canvases is UNDERSTATED -- which strengthens K1 rather than weakening it."
  },
